course: dictionary
lesson: 5956
title: Tiny words, big clues
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can mean a small box, and it can also describe something very small. Context tells you which meaning is right. «Stretched out, the DNA from one tiny cell would be about two metres long, so it is wound up very tightly, like a garden hose coiled into a matchbox.» The words tiny, wound up tightly and coiled tell you that a matchbox here means a very small space, not a box of matches.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. If you read «coiled into a small box that holds matches», the sentence sounds odd, because a garden hose cannot fit inside a box of matches. So the sentence is telling you about size, not about matches.
explain: Some words take on new meanings in phrases. A «matchbox car» is a tiny toy car, and a «matchbox flat» is a tiny home. When you see matchbox in front of another word, check whether it names a real box or describes something very small.
fact: A matchbox is a small box that holds matches, with a rough side for striking them.
fact: «Matchbox» can also mean something very small, such as a «matchbox car» (a tiny toy car).
fact: A «matchbox flat» means a very tiny home.
fact: Matches are for adults. If you find matches or a matchbox, give them to an adult straight away.
exercise: «Stretched out, the DNA from one tiny cell would be about two metres long, so it is wound up very tightly, like a garden hose coiled into a matchbox.» What does matchbox suggest about size? | Very large, like a bus | Very wet | Very loud | *Very small
exercise: Maya finds a matchbox in the park. What should she do? | *Give it to an adult | Hide it under a bush | Strike a match to see if it works | Keep it in her pocket for later
exercise: Tom says, «My favourite toy is a matchbox car.» What is a matchbox car? | *A tiny toy car | A box that holds matches | A car that runs on matches | A real car made of wood
test: In the story, the family lived in a matchbox flat. What does matchbox flat mean? | A flat with a huge garden | A flat made of wood | A flat on the top floor of a tall building | *A tiny home
test: Ben wants to find out how much space a small box holds. Which maths skill does he need? | *Measuring volume | Spelling | Drawing maps | Singing
exam: Which is the safe thing to do if you find matches at a friend's house? | Keep them as a treasure | *Give them to an adult | Hide them in your bag | Strike one to test it
